<Text>&lt;font color="#000000" size=11&gt;

The &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Checkbox&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control is a special type of button with an on/off state.
This state is usually visually represented with a box containing a check mark, but a separate &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Visual&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; could be created to make it appear raised/indented.
Here is an example &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Checkbox&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control:

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

The &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Radio Button&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; controls work in conjunction with a &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Radio Group&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; control.
The &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Radio Group&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; is a container object, similar to a &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scene&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;, and has special behavior which modifies the state of its contained controls.

</Text>
</Properties>
</XuiHtmlElement>
